#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Verify and fix metadata for a music library laid out as:

    <root>/<artist>/<album>/<song>.<ext>

Artist and album tags are trusted from the folder structure. Title and
track number are looked up primarily via a MusicBrainz text search on
that trusted artist/album, matched against whatever the filename gives
us: a filename like "Track 3" or "03 - Song" yields a track number,
matched by position against the release's tracklist; otherwise the
remaining filename text is fuzzy-matched against candidate titles.
Only when that search can't place the file with confidence does it
fall back to AcoustID audio fingerprinting, which is prone to confusing
similar-sounding versions of a song (e.g. instrumental vs. vocal) that
the filename/tracklist match above tells apart just fine.

The recording's full MusicBrainz artist credit (main artist plus any
featured artists) is written to a separate multi-value "artists" tag,
alongside the single folder-trusted "artist" tag, which is left untouched.

Recognition is slow and rate-limited, so nothing is written to disk
directly -- planned changes are queued to a YAML file for review, optionally
sanity-checked with --check (which walks through any likely mistakes it
finds and asks what to do about each one), then applied with --apply.
Neither --check nor --apply calls the APIs.

Album art is a separate mode (--album-art): for each album directory, a
MusicBrainz release search finds the release, its cover is fetched from
the Cover Art Archive, scaled to 300x300, and saved as "art.jpg" (or a
filename passed to --album-art), overwriting it if already present.

A ".mmfignore" file in root, if present, excludes matching files/folders
from every pass (recognition, --check, --apply, --rename, --album-art),
using the same pattern syntax as ".gitignore".

Setup:
    pip install mutagen pyacoustid musicbrainzngs pyyaml pillow pathspec
    # provides `fpcalc`, used by pyacoustid:
    sudo apt install libchromaprint-tools

    # Get a free AcoustID API key (no cost, just a signup):
    # https://acoustid.org/new-application
    export MMF_ACOUSTID_API_KEY=your_key_here

Usage:
    music_metafix /path/to/music/root

    # optionally, sanity-check temp/changes.yml before applying it:
    music_metafix --check temp/changes.yml

    # review/edit temp/changes.yml, then:
    music_metafix /path/to/music/root --apply temp/changes.yml

    # separately, rename files based on their (now-corrected) tags:
    music_metafix /path/to/music/root --rename "%num - %title"

    # separately, whenever you want to (re)fetch cover art:
    music_metafix /path/to/music/root --album-art
    music_metafix /path/to/music/root --album-art cover.jpg

Queue file paths are relative to root, so --apply needs the same root
passed alongside it to resolve them.
"""

